    "title": "Dad recalls the horror moment his daughter was struck down by a car on their way to church in Stafford Heights",
    "text": "By Max Aldred for Daily Mail Australia\nPublished: 07:56 GMT, February 9, 2025 | Updated: 08:31 GMT, February 9, 2025\nA father opened on the heartbreaking moment that his daughter’s hand escaped his moments before he was hit by a vehicle on his way to the church.\nThe slow movement vehicle hit the 11 -year -old girl while crossing the road with her family in Appleby Road, Stafford Heights north of Brisbane on Sunday morning.\nThe horrible incident developed outside the Baptist Church Stafford Heights, where the family was about to attend the weekly sermon.\nThe girl was treated in the scene by facial injuries before being urgently taken to the Queensland Children’s Hospital in a stable condition.\n‘My daughter left my hands and the car has hit her. I don’t know what happened, ‘t sui dun told him Messaging mail .\n“She is in the hospital now, okay, her right jaw has scars and pasta.”\nThe accident was developed in front of the parishioners, including pastor Cungbik Kingbawl.\nA girl was urgently taken to the hospital after she was hit by a slow movement vehicle outside her church.\nThe girl suffered facial injuries and was taken to the hospital, where she remains in a stable condition\n“They were crossing the road here, I arrived there and I saw the driver,” he said in reference to a pedestrian island in the middle of the road, “the shepherd told the publication.\nHe added that the Church would be praying for the family following the accident.\nThe Church organizes masses for ‘Congregations of the people of Chin de Myanmar’, on Sundays, according to its website.\nIt is believed that the driver of the vehicle remained in the scene for a short period of time, but he left before emergency services arrived.\nThe driver left his phone number with witnesses on the scene.\nQueensland police have launched an investigation into the cause of the accident.\nShare or comment on this article: Dad remembers the moment of horror that her daughter was attacked by a car on her way to the church in Stafford Heightts\n(Tagstotranslate) Dailymail (T) News (T) Brisbane",
